[49m[38;5;10m+      1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Phase B — valid-path differential tests, gated on `CONFIGS.md`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Every one of the 128 `CONFIGS.md` rows is the cross product
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `i (2) x layer (4) x k (16)`. For each row the bits the C never uses
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! (`h[0]`, `h[1]` bit0, `h[2]`'s low nibble) are randomized with a fixed seed,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! so a row only passes if it holds across all the values that must not matter.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Both implementations are reached exclusively through their `.so` exports.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
